# windows-conemu -- the terminfo entry this renderer's contract is written against.
#
# GENERATED-DERIVED copy of org/jline/utils/windows-conemu.caps as shipped by jline, which is the file that
# is actually READ at run time (terminal/src/main/resources in the source tree, and inside lib/JLine3.jar in
# the install). This one exists so that `tic`/`infocmp` -- tools that will not parse the jline spelling, whose
# first line carries prose with commas in it -- can be run against the same capability set. terminfo_check.sh
# proves the two sets are identical and refuses the build if they are not; it also compares the on-disk caps
# with the copy inside lib/JLine3.jar, because "the entry we audited" and "the entry that ships" are two facts.
#
# The rules that decide what is IN here live in ../TERMINFO.md (and the renderer's own dispositions in
# ../ANSI_SUPPORTS.md); the short version of why the omissions are as deliberate as the additions:
#
#   cbt, hts, tbc          -- no tab-stop state exists yet (ESC H is ignored), so CSI Z has nowhere to back
#                             up to. Item #70: the table is approved and not built; when it lands these three
#                             go in and `it#8` stops being the whole story.
#   smir, rmir, mir        -- IRM has no body in either parser, so CSI @ always inserts regardless.
#   smam, rmam             -- DECAWM is modelled (#61) but the entry also describes sessions ConEmu's own
#                             parser reads, where its SetConsoleMode is commented out (Ansi.cpp:3268-3281);
#                             declaring the pair would be a claim about the OTHER reader (DESIGN I26).
#   smkx, rmkx             -- DECCKM is an input-side mode and this terminal's input is console records.
#   blink, invis, nv       -- SGR 5/6/8 hold no state on either leg.
#   rmp, sgr10/sgr11 arms  -- no alternate-font path.
#   mc5p                   -- no printer.
#   flash                  -- ESC g flashes the ConEmu window; a renderer must not, and leaving it out makes
#                             readers fall back to bel.
#   initc, ccc             -- OSC 4/10/11 now change the palette (#55), but the entry also describes a session
#                             parsed by ConEmu, which consumes them and changes nothing (I26 again).
#   xenl                   -- measured absent on both writer legs; it is the whole reason `am` is declared.
#   kf13 and up, kLFT/kRIT/kUP/kDN/kHOM/kEND/kPRV/kNXT/kIC/kDC
#                          -- jline's key leg synthesises the bytes for a modified key itself and never asks
#                             caps; terminfo can name only the Shift arm, no widget binds a shifted key.
#   u8, u9                 -- CSI c and CSI >c are BOTH answered, but no code in jline reads user8/user9
#                             (CursorSupport reads user6 and user7 only), so a value here would be invented.
#
# Inedits: kbs=^H stays because jline decodes it through Curses.tputs to 0x08 and binds 0x08 and 0x7f to the
# same widget, and all three Windows entries in this jline spell it that way. rep is in because CSI b has a
# body in the parser and a model in the renderer; its parameter must reach tputs as an INT, because
# toInteger() parses a Character as a String and throws. u6/u7 are in because the answer leg writes the reply
# back onto CONIN$ as key events in the shape CursorSupport compiles u6 into a regex for.
#
windows-conemu|ConEmu ANSI with the native renderer (no xenl: margin wrap is immediate; bce: every erase fills with the live attribute),
	am, bce, msgr,
	colors#256, cols#80, it#8, lines#24, pairs#64,
	bel=^G, bold=\E[1m, clear=\E[H\E[2J,
	cr=^M, cub=\E[%p1%dD, cub1=\E[D, cud=\E[%p1%dB, cud1=\E[B,
	cuf=\E[%p1%dC, cuf1=\E[C, cup=\E[%i%p1%d;%p2%dH,
	cuu=\E[%p1%dA, cuu1=\E[A,
	civis=\E[?25l, cnorm=\E[?25h, cvvis=\E[?25h,
	smcup=\E[?1049h, rmcup=\E[?1049l,
	rc=\E8, sc=\E7,
	il=\E[%p1%dL, il1=\E[L,
	dl=\E[%p1%dM, dl1=\E[M,
	ich=\E[%p1%d@, ich1=\E[@, dch=\E[%p1%dP, dch1=\E[P, ech=\E[%p1%dX, rep=%p1%c\E[%p2%{1}%-%db,
	el=\E[K, ed=\E[J, el1=\E[1K,
	home=\E[H, hpa=\E[%i%p1%dG, vpa=\E[%i%p1%dd,
	ind=^J, indn=\E[%p1%dS, rin=\E[%p1%dT, ri=\EM, nel=\EE, ht=^I,
	csr=\E[%i%p1%d;%p2%dr,
	kbs=^H, kcbt=\E[Z,
	kcub1=\EOD, kcud1=\EOB, kcuf1=\EOC, kcuu1=\EOA,
	khome=\E[H,
	op=\E[39;49m,
	rev=\E[7m,
	smacs=\E(0, rmacs=\E(B, acsc=``aaffggiijjkkllmmnnooppqqrrssttuuvvwwxxyyzz{{||}}~~,
	rmso=\E[27m, rmul=\E[24m, smso=\E[7m, smul=\E[4m,
	setab=\E[48;5;%p1%dm, setaf=\E[38;5;%p1%dm,
	sgr=\E[0%?%p6%t;1%;%?%p2%t;4%;%?%p1%p3%|%t;7%;m,
	sgr0=\E(B\E[0m,
	u6=\E[%i%d;%dR, u7=\E[6n,
	kdch1=\E[3~, kich1=\E[2~, kend=\E[4~, knp=\E[6~, kpp=\E[5~,
	kf1=\EOP, kf2=\EOQ, kf3=\EOR, kf4=\EOS, kf5=\E[15~, kf6=\E[17~,
	kf7=\E[18~, kf8=\E[19~, kf9=\E[20~, kf10=\E[21~, kf11=\E[23~, kf12=\E[24~,
